      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can name this `fDstReadBounds` and it\u0027ll represent the area of the dst target that will be read, regardless of what the strategy is. We can then use its emptiness value when handling the texture-sampling approach, and makes the `CommandBuffer::addRenderPass` signature simpler because you always just pass in the dst read bounds. If the strategy is texture-sample, it looks at non-empty. If it\u0027s texture-copy, it uses it as is, if it\u0027s fb fetch it just ignores it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "9aa449324fa3fe99157ab66dc6252f1fa3f12668",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
